    "question": {
      ":question/id": "932654c7-97a3-5bef-934c-b50f7157cfaa",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 7 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of $a_{11}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 7 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+2C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{1}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}+2C_{1}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
