      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of $a_{31}=5$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 15 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-3C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 17 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+2C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 17 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{2}:=C_{2}-3C_{1}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}+2C_{1}$.",
